> Actually, given that the problem is occurring in sysgen, better
> advice would be to see if sysgen knows about this card.  Here are
> a few blocks from a dump of sysgen.exe (V5.5-2):

SYSGEN is supposed to take the first and last letters from the beginning
of the module ID in the TURBOchannel ID ROM to form the name of the driver
for the module. If you have a module that identifies itself as a PMAG-BA,
for example, SYSGEN should be looking for PGDRIVER.EXE.

Of course, it might know more about DEC modules and only do this for modules
it doesn't recognize...
