There's a COM file that's something like SYPAGSWPFILES.COM (I'm 
doing this from memory and havne't done it for a while, so that might
not quite be it) that gets executed early in the boot process and can
be used to install a page file from another disk if there is no
pagefile on the system disk.   What you could do for "if the disk is
unavailable" is this:

1: put your primary page and swap files on the second disk and install
them with SYPAGSWPFILES.COM 

2: Also create a secondary page/swap file on the system disk that isn't
installed unless the first install is unsuccessful.

Implementation via DCL is left as an exercise... 

