>recognised,
>2) have the CTRL/ALT/SHIFT/CAPS-LOCK keys mapped properly?  (BTW, I'm
>running
>VMS V6.1)
>

  It uses a "standard" PS2 style PC keyboard.  The important thing is
  that it fully implement the key sets - in particular scan set 3.
  In this mode the keyboard generates a unique code per key.  We set
  the keyboard into up/down for all keys.

  (Digital UNIX does the same thing, so if you find one for UNIX,
   it will work on OpenVMS).

  Screwy mappings are the norm however... see the release notes.
  To map the keyboard to match the engravings (by default it's in a
  VT-style remapping) select Options/Keyboard and select a LK444/443
  keymap with a _PC postfix.


