jmorriso@Master.ConcordPacific.Com (John Paul Morrison) writes:
:
:Anyone know the pinouts for the modular (MMJ) plug used on
:a vt320 terminal? 

  It's not RS232, it's DEC-423.  Here are the DEC-423 MMJ pinouts:

	  1 data terminal ready
	  2 transmitted data
	  3 transmitted data return
	  4 recieved data return
	  5 received data
	  6 data set ready

  The H8571-B adapter allows one to convert from a BC16-E DECconnect MMJ
  cable to an RS232 female connector, and the H8571-C converts it to an
  RS232 male -- pins visible and recessed into the connector; due to the
  recess, some folks call this connector the female, though it is refered
  to as the male connector in most/all Digital documents I am aware of.

  Parts, manuals and DECconnect catalogs are available from 1-800-DIGITAL.

