We need to connect 5 RS422 serial lines running at 38400 baud
to a DEC Alpha AXP 2100.  Ideally we would like an off-the-shelf
solution for both hardware and software.  We have considered
several alternative solutions, but none seem entirely suitable:

1. The DIGIboard PC/8 EISA board is supported by VMS, but is only
   RS232, and may impose an excessive load on the Alpha processor.
   Does anyone have any processor load figures, or any experience
   of using this board at high baud rates (in both directions)?

2. The Comptrol Hostess HO186 board (basically an 80186 processor
   plus either two or four 8530 SCCs).  This is not supported by VMS,
   so we would have to write driver software in order to use it.
   Also, can an 80186 processor running at 8Mhz handle the required
   data rate?  Perhaps we could sub-contract the software development
   to a software house.  Can anyone recommend one with expertise in
   this area?  Does anyone have performance figures for this board
   or something similar?

3. A terminal server.  Supported by VMS, but all the terminal servers
   found so far are RS232.  Does anyone know of a terminal server
   with an RS422 option?

I would be interested to hear from anyone with information about these,
or who can suggest an alternative solution.
-- 
Paul Dewhirst



