Hi.I just read wbout your PDP11 problem. First, when you boot, do you
get any indication on the terminal as to the OS that's loading, like
RT-11, RSX-11M, etc.? Unfortunately, back in the '11 days, some folks
were really daring and rolled their own operating system. We had a
library management system that was that way. Yecch. If it's a standard
DEC OS, perhaps you can modify your boot process (RT can boot from
floppy) to get at the file system.

Failing that, does your system allow for viewing "the next record", so
as to effectively scroll through the whole database? If so, you could
put together a PC program to emulate the VT220 and catch the data and
save it as a formatted ASCII file. Visual Basic and PDQComm (from
Crescent Software) makes this kind of thing relatively painless.

Hope this helps,
