newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


    Andreas --

    Here's some data for your chart:

    The 21064A has been called the EV45 inside Digital.

    The AlphaStation 250 4/266 uses a 128-bit path to memory (the APECS
    chip set available from Digital allows either 64 or 128 bits, by using
    a different number of Decade data path chips).  I suspect that the EV4
    could do the same, since it uses the same chipset.

    The EV45 has 16 kBytes of primary instruction cache and 16 kBytes of
    primary data cache.

    The EV5 has 16 kBytes of primary instruction cache and 16 kBytes of
    primary data cache.  It also has 96 kBytes of three-way set-associative
    second-level cache on chip.

