In article <3ujmvm$br4@explorer.csc.com>, rmsmith@csc.com (Robert Smith) writes:
|>Can I use a dual system DSSI connection (Vax3400 and uVaxII (630Q)
|>tied via DSSI to disks?

Sure.  The uVAXII would need a KFQSA Qbus-to-DSSI adapter added.  Both systems
will be able to access the DSSI devices simultaneously.

Because the KFQSA looks like a disk adapter to the host rather than a PA port
like the uVAX 3400's integral DSSI adapter, it can't pass SCS traffic between
the two CPUs, so the Ethernet will be used for inter-CPU SCS traffic
(connection manager, lock manager, OPCOM, etc.) instead of DSSI, but this
shouldn't matter much in your case.

You may want to put a quorum disk on the DSSI so either node can run alone
if necessary.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Keith B. Parris, StorageWorks Host-Based Software Team, Digital Equip. Corp.

