>DECserver 100 to a VAXstation 3100/10.  Here is the configuration.
>
>        DECserver 100 (DSRVA-AA)        VAXstation 3100/10
>        Terminal Server software V1.3   VAX/VMS V5.4-3
>
>The software installed without error; however, when the DECserver is turned on
>the following error message is produced.
>
>        DECnet event 0.7, aborted service request
>        From node 11.221 (CHANGO), 18-JUL-1995 08:58:32.05
>        Circuit SVA-0, Line open error

There is no such thing as a VAXstation 3100/10.  The lowest VAXstation 3100
model is 30, but there is a MicroVAX 3100 Model 10.  Both have similar boxes,
Ethernet controllers, and connectors.

There is a good chance you should believe the line open error.  How much do you
know about Ethernet configuration?  If it's thinwire, you need a T connector at
all nodes and a terminator on both ends; you don't just plug the thinwire cable
into the last node's BNC connector.  The 3100 has two Ethernet connectors, and
you have to throw a little switch to select the right one.  If you're using
thickwire, connecting the taps is always frought with excitement.  And of
course, there are lots of other configuration rules and opportunities for
connectors to be plugged almost all of the way in.

