In article <1995Jul18.123716.10622@eisner>, lubell@eisner.decus.org (Bradford A Lubell) writes:
>I inherited some OLD hardware which I am attempting to make work.  The budget
>is zero ($0.00) so upgrading is not an option.  I am attempting to connect a
>DECserver 100 to a VAXstation 3100/10.  Here is the configuration.
>
>        DECserver 100 (DSRVA-AA)        VAXstation 3100/10
>        Terminal Server software V1.3   VAX/VMS V5.4-3
>
>The software installed without error; however, when the DECserver is turned on
>the following error message is produced.
>
>        DECnet event 0.7, aborted service request
>        From node 11.221 (CHANGO), 18-JUL-1995 08:58:32.05
>        Circuit SVA-0, Line open error
>

After you installed the software there is some setup needed to make tell the
VAXstation to recognized MOM/MOP boot requests from the DECserver.  It looks
like at least part of this has not been done.  I believe you'll find a
SYS$SYSROOT:[DECSERVER] directory.  The logical MOM$LOAD should be DEFINEd
(/SYSTEM/EXEC) to point to MOM$SYSTEM and then SYS$SYSROOT:[DECSERVER] during
system boot.  The command file SYS$SYSROOT:[DECSERVER]DSVCONFIG.COM should set
up everything else for you.  In NCP, verify that the DECserver has been given a
node entry with a hardware address and loader information (three parameters, if
I recall correctly).  Also verify that circuit SVA-0 has been DEFINEd and SET
to have service enabled.

