In article <tvg.16.00143191@ccphys.nsu.nsk.su>, tvg@ccphys.nsu.nsk.su writes:
|>  Please...
|>
|>  Could anyone tell the differences between DEUNA and DELUA Ethernets?
|>We have no manuals for both. I know they are software compatible because 
|>DEUNA driver in 4.3 BSD works with DELUA pretty well. Are there some 
|>differences in productivity? Maybe one is more suitable for some tasks and 
|>another for others?

The DEUNA is the original UNIBUS Ethernet module (2 hex boards with a
T11 PDP-11 controlling it and all MSI and SSI logic implementing the
controller).  The DELUA is a reengineered module with a 68000 and a 
"modern" Ethernet Controller (I think it used the LANCE).

The DELUA is by far the faster of the two.  The DEUNA could achieve
about 3Mb/s with a tail wind.  The DELUA could much more than that.

