Hi!

To send VMSmail to an ALL-IN-1 user use the following syntax:

To: MRGATE::"A1::A1user"

Remote, VMSmail Gateway on local node:

To: MRGATE::"node::A1::A1user"

VMSmail Gateway on remote node:

To: node::MRGATE::"A1::A1user"

A1 is the name of the mailbox and could have been defined otherwise.


From A DCL command procedure you can use:

$ notify := MANAGER     ! ALL-IN-1 user to receive mail
.
.
.
$! Send the mail
$!
$ mail/subject="Subject of the mail" vms-filename.ext MRGATE::"A1::''notify'"


Or if you prefer to send it from ALL-IN-1:

$ ALLIN1/NOINIT/REENTER
oa$ini_init
cabinet open
get #to1 = "A1user1"
get #to2 = "A1user2"
get #subject = "Subject of the mail"
get #file = "vms-filename.ext"
mail push
mail create/open/nosend
mail to #to1
mail to #to2
mail subject #subject
mail close_message
copy #file oa$curdoc_filename
mail send
cabinet refile_document, oa$wastebasket
mail pop
exit
$ EXIT


There is also a User's Guide for the VMSmail Gateway that covers this.

Hope this helps. Ciao ... Pierangelo (Gigi) Loreggia, Switzerland




