David M. Desroches was both correct and incorrect in his reply.  ALL-IN-1 is
designed to be friendly for screen operations but does has several ways to
provide access and support in a DCL command procedure.  ALL-IN-1 has spent its
entire lifetime being under estimated in terms of features and ability to
provide value to normal humans so the misunderstanding was not unusual.  (':

Here is an example of sending a message containing the SYS$LOGIN:TMP.TMP file
to BIG_BOSS and THE_JERK (who, of course would be two different people in your
nicknames ;') with a title of "The latest sales information":

$ ALLIN1/REENTER/TERMINAL=HARDCOPY /SCRIPT=SYS$LOGIN:BATCH_IT.SCP

Where SYS$LOGIN:BATCH_IT.SCP looks a lot like:

! Created using Learn Mode on 19-Jul-1995, at 10:47pm
!
!		Transfer the file into the ALL-IN-1 file cabinet
DT RV {CR}
SYS$LOGIN:TMP.TMP {CR}
{UP}
SALES REPORTS {DOWN}
The latest sales information {CR}
!
!		Go to Electronic Mail and forward the document
em {CR}
sel SALES REPORTS {CR}
f {CR}
BIG_BOSS {CR}
THE_JERK {CR}
{CR}
{CR}
{DOWN}
N {CR}
s {CR}
!
! [End BATCH_IT.SCP]

As the first line of the BATCH_IT.SCP shows, I created the script using the
learn feature which is invoked via CTRL/L in modern versions of ALL-IN-1.

Have fun,
don

