In article <1995Jul19.125250.10629@eisner>, lubell@eisner.decus.org (Bradford A Lubell) writes:
|> [..]
|>    o NCP CONNECT NODE fails with "Target does not respond"

The NCP CONNECT command attempts to connect to the DECserver's remote
console using the MOP protocol.  If the DECserver has not booted, then
this remote console is not available as the software that implements it
is in the DECserver downline load image - not the DECserver ROMs.

|>    o DS100 does not respond to its terminal lines.

Seems to also indicate that the DECserver is not booted.

|>    o Verify that H4005 used by the DS100 is in place properly.  This is an
|>      old thick wire set-up.  Is it possible for a H4005 to work only in
|>      part?

In networks, I have learned that anything is possible :-).

|>    o Continue looking for V2.0 of the software (that is apparently the
|>      newest version)

Yes, in particular, if you can get V2.0 BL23B, you will have the very
latest.

|>    o Connect a terminal to port 1 of the DS100.  Anybody know what
|>      communication charateristics would be.

I believe the default port characteristics for plugging a terminal into
port 1 are something like 9600, 8 bit characters, no parity.  Port 1 is
the 'console' port so boot errors (and possibly other hardware failures)
that are detected should be displayed on any terminal connected to port 1.

-- 
