X-Deja-AN: 106584691
references: <3ujn22$bvb@explorer.csc.com>
organization: University of Guelph
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec

Robert Smith (rmsmith@csc.com) wrote:
: Is it possible to set up a uVax II (BA123) with two CPUs in the box/
: on the bus?
Yep, but you don't want to do it:-) The result is a weird non-shared memory
multiprocessor. The slave cpus only see the 1Mbyte of memory on them
(the master sees its 1Mbyte + expansion memory cards, but not the 1Mbyte
 chunks on the slaves). The only way the cpus can share memory is by
mapping it to the qbus and memory access times through the qbus are SLOW!!
(There is also a 4Mbyte - 8K address space limit for the q22)

Have fun, rick




