David S. Loose-Mitchell (dloose@farmr1.med.uth.tmc.edu) wrote:
: Does anyone have ant information on installing a third party SCSI drive 
: on an AlphaServer running OSF 3.2? DEC wants about $1050 for a 1Gb drive, 
: which could be either a Seagate or a Quantum. Comparably sized drives on 
: the open market sell for about $450.00. The problem is in configuring the 
: drives since only a limited number of geometries are supported in 
: /etc/disktab. Is OSF "open" enough that one can correctly install a 
: non-DEC drive?

We put non-DEC drives in all the time.  You can just add your own entries
to disktab (intelligently if you actually know the geometry, but most of
that stuff is only used as hits to the filesystem creation routine to
optimize the disk layout, the only one that trully matters is the number
of sectors).

We've been gobbling up the 2 and 4 gig seagates with a voracious appetite
and haven't found a machine here (Sparc, PC, HP, or Alpha) that we couldn't
get them to work on.

-Ron



