In article <3ujn22$bvb@explorer.csc.com>, rmsmith@csc.com (Robert Smith) writes...
>Is it possible to set up a uVax II (BA123) with two CPUs in the box/
>on the bus?
>thanks in advance
>bob
> 
Yes, it is possible.  In particular, there is hardware support for
multiprocessing in the form of a interprocessor communications
register (ICR).  Multiprocessing through multiple KA630's  isn't
supported by any release of VMS I know of, and there are difficulties
regarding termination once you get past two processors.  (I seem to
recall some custom setups using four KA630's, but having to split
the configuration into two BA11-S boxes.)

For more information, you can use anonymous ftp to

  sunsite.unc.edu

to go to the directory

  /pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/hardware/micronotes/numerical

and get the file

  micronote.026

which will give you some of the rudimentary technical details involved.

Tim. (shoppa@altair.krl.caltech.edu)



