start to check the windoze stuff FIRST, 'cause this is with 
>90% ceartainty the reason.

Just my experience with MS-"ware", though.......
....but to make sure I'd try to set the 1152 up at a serial port,
and copy a file (single text or proven correct PS) to it from DOS.

In that case there are NO windoze-then-crash drivers involved. If it's 
only with PS-files, then maybe you're just ran out of PS-Mem in the printer?
If you have lots of graphics on a simple page the memory just might be too 
small (this problem I have sometime here, with 1152 as well as HP4+). 
My VMS-System then TELLS ME why the job did not print correctly, 99% sure 
doze or windoze doesn't...

If it works as described above, go back to parallel and try again without 
windoze. If it does work, the it's not the printer!

BTW, don't assume that any given windoze-app will create 
up-to-standard postscript for testing the postscript interpreter in any
printer! 

Happy printing!

Uwe


