State of the art processor: 21164, aka EV5, 250-300 Mhz, quad issue
Cache size 8+8+96KB on chip (L1 instruction, L1 data, 3-way set associative L2) 
Off-chip cache sizes supported are 0 to 64MB

Digital has presently announced 3 servers that employ the 21164.  All of
these provide 4MB L3 cache:

         Model                   Mhz  Max CPUs  SPECint92  SPECfp92

         AlphaServer 2100 5/250  250     4        277.0     410.4
         AlphaServer 8200 5/300  300     6        341.4     512.9
         AlphaServer 8400 5/300  300    12        341.4     512.9

Digital has not yet announced workstations that employ the 21164.  The
fastest announced workstations use the 21064A, a shrink/speedup of the
original 21064.  The 21064A caches are 16+16KB I+D L1 on-chip and up to
8MB L2 off-chip.  The top of the workstation line is:

         Model                   Mhz  L2 cache SPECint92  SPECfp92

         AlphaStation 250 4/266  266    2MB       198.6      262.5
         DEC 3000 Model 900      275    2MB       178.4      244.6

The AlphaStation uses PCI, the DEC 3000 uses Turbochannel. 

