I'm looking for some advice about network diagnostic equipment.

We have a 60 (and growing) node Decnet/pathwork network.  Last
year when we set up our 95 budget, we put in some money for 
"network diagnostic equipment".  The problem is, with all the
hardware and software components available, I'm not sure
exactly what we should be trying to get.

Here's what our system has:
Two Vax servers, a Vaxstation, an X-terminal, 60 PC's.
The PC's are linked using Pathworks (4.x, converting to V5).
We use thinwire coax, running Decnet, Lat, MOP, no tcp/ip (yet-
possibly next year).
All the thinwire is off of a DEMPR thinwire repeater, the DEMPR
and the vaxes are hooked into a DELNI AUI "hub".

What I'm looking to get:
- An ability to show the load on the network.
- Something to show if we have any trouble spots with the wiring,
    like excessive retries from a given node, collisions, etc.
- If a problem develops, I'd like to have a way to narrow down
    the problem, to the NIC, cable, etc.
- We do our own cable installing, so it would be nice to have a TDR
    capability.

