    Hmm, the DECmate II was a desktop (a BIG desktop by today's standards),
    not a tower.

    The processor is a Harris 6120, which is a PDP8 clone.  There's also an
    optional Intel coprocessor.  The PDP8 side comes with 64k twelve-bit
    word memory (the max it can handle).  Eight MHz operation, dropping to
    five MHz during I/O if I recall correctly.  It uses ST506 hard disks,
    such as Digital's RD50 (all of five MBytes, which seemed like a lot at
    the time), and an RX50 dual 5-1/4" floppy drive.  Operating systems
    included WPS-8 (word processing system), OS-278 and CP/M-86.

    Check over in alt.sys.pdp8.

