In article <3u61e5$o8j@lll-winken.llnl.gov>, oberman@icaen.llnl.gov wrote:

> SQE Test (not SQL) must be enabled for all DTE. But the integral interface is
> internal, so SQE Test is not applicable. SQE Test is a signal from the MAU
> (transceiver) to the AUI interface (the 15 pin connector) and simply does not
> exist on an internal interface where there is no MAU.
> 

I can vouch for this. I've just taken over running a collection of VAX and
Alpha systems, all of which had tiny twisted-pair to AUI converter boxes
connected. I had to enable SQE Test on each and every one of them, lest
the DECnet Show Known Lines display indicate a "Carrier Detect Check
Failure" that goes up in lock step with every packet transmitted. 
Enabling SQE makes this go away.

John Francini



