Subject: PDP/VAX Hardware help file: chopped up and categorized for archival
Date: 1995/07/06
Message-ID: <3tfrbl$22d@umbc8.umbc.edu>
X-Deja-AN: 105730606
organization: University of Maryland, Baltimore County
newsgroups: vmsnet.pdp-11,comp.sys.dec

Greetings!

After obtaining a copy of the hardware_help.txt (Decuserve articles)
file from Tim Shoppa's PDP-11 archive on sunsite.unc.edu, I found that
there was a lot of useful information in that file, for both PDPs
(mostly PDP-11s, but some PDP-8 info as well :-) ) and VAXen; it was
all bottled up in one large 5MB text file, however.  I noticed that
there were two hardware_help.txt files, in different directories, but
they both seemed to contain about the same information, so I grabbed a
copy of the larger of the two for my exercise in file chopping.

Basically, what I intended to do was separate the PDP and VAX related
files.  What I ended up doing was to create lots of individual text
files, one file for each topic; the PDP related files in one
directory, files related to VAXen in another directory.  Of course,
there is some overlap, since there are some files which pertain to
both types of systems.  I tried to put the vax-only files in the vax
directory and anything that pertained in any way to the PDP-11s (or
PDP-8s) in the pdp directory.

It seems that I've extracted just about all of the useful PDP related
information (except, perhaps, for a few bits pertaining more to
printers than PDPs) from it.  Quite a good bit of the VAX related
information was extracted as well, but I've not finished with that.

Other things: I've also gone through the Decuserve files pertaining to
RT-11, RSX, etc. and broken them up as well... more on that later.

If others would also find the files resulting from the chopping up of
this file to be useful, I'll add the files to my PDP-11 archive in a
few days.  If anyone would find a *.tar.gz file of all these files to
be useful, I'll be glad to arrange that as well.  

Thanks, very much, to those who posted the information to Decuserve
and those who archived that information!

