>do the same warnings exist on TA90/TA90E tape drives? We are having no 
>problems writing our backups, but the rmu/backup/verify pass of our full 
>database backups fail consistently. Our FE ran diags on the system, 
>cleaned the heads, etc and came up with nothing but that he was 
>suspecting that the Black Watch tapes were our problem.
> 
>Any one else out there with any insight / suggestions???

It's awfully hard to diagnose this sort of problem at a distance without
all of the information that you've presumabley looked at.  What is the
error message that the backups give upon failing?  What entries go into
the error log?  (Clearly, you're going to have to enable error logging
for the tape device if you haven't already done so.)  Doing a
$SHOW DEV/FULL on the tape drive both before and after the error can
also give some useful information.

All I can say about BlackWatch tapes is that 9-track BlackWatch tapes
work wonderfully for me, despite all the warnings DEC gives about them.

Tim. (shoppa@altair.krl.caltech.edu)



