>although i checked ewa0_mode value before the booting,
>the on-screen message from the boot process says 
>that tu0 (the interface connected to ethernet) takes
>the value AUI.

    You have to issue the INIT console command (or cycle power) after
    setting the EWA0_MODE environment variable, or it won't be seen by the
    operating system.  Is it possible that this step was skipped?

    	>>> set ewa0_mode twisted-pair
    	>>> init

