That's exactly the point. Look at any of the commercial license managers,
they'll set you back 5 to 10000 $ easily. That figure often doesn't include
support several platforms, they cost extra. Also, experiences from other
software companies in the field that I spoke to were that users get pretty
confused when they have to configure license manager daemons all over. Next,
my application is running on 9 different platforms by now, with 3-5 more
in the pipeline. I don't want to run a different manager on each system,
that's a support nightmare.
