> to know all the specs.
> -CPU type and speed.

Intersil 6120, a PDP-8 on a chip. There is also a CP/M coprocessor for the
DECmate II; if your DECmate II has it, there's a Z80 in addition to the 6120.

> -Memeory requirments.

It has 32Kwords of memory for the PDP-8 (plus some extra for screen memory
and "slushware"). If you have the Z80, there's an additional 64KB for the
Z80.

> -Harddisk compatibility.

Good luck finding a hard disk controller. If you do, it can take MFM disks.
The official supported disks are the RD50 (a 5MB 5.25" disk) and the RD51
(a 10MB 5.25" disk). Other disks can be supported, but you will either have
to write or find a formatter for them.

> -etc.

There is software available on the net, but I forget where. The good folks over
on alt.sys.pdp8 can help you out...
