Alex Tang (altitude@umich.edu) wrote:
: Hi gang.

: I've got a VRC-21A 21" monitor but I don't have the manual.

: Can someone tell me what the buttons on the front do?  Actually, I would
: like to know what the combinations of lights on the front control panel
: mean.  

: There are 5 lights, each seems to stand for a different mode.  From left
: to right they are labeled:

:   Horizontal location
:   Horizontal Size
:   Vertical Location
:   Vertical Size
:   3 dots (has to do with color).

: The big problem is that you can sometimes combinations of lights appear,
: and they have some completely different meaning.  

: Can someone tell me what the combo's mean? 


ON  OFF OFF OFF OFF - H Position (moves picture left or right)
OFF ON  OFF OFF OFF - H Size (narrows or widens picture)
OFF OFF ON  OFF OFF - V Position (moves picture up and down)
OFF OFF OFF ON  OFF - V Size (shrinks or expands height of picture)
BL  OFF OFF OFF ON  - Color 1 (Factory preset to 9300 K white temperature)
  (You switch between Color2, and 3 by using the +/- button when on color 1).
OFF BL  OFF OFF ON  - Color 2 (Factory preset to 6500 K white temperature)
OFF OFF BL  OFF ON  - Color 3 control (Adjusts the white color balance,
								default 9300K)
ON  ON  OFF OFF ON  - Color 3 Green Gain
OFF ON  ON  OFF ON  - Color 3 Blue Gain
OFF OFF ON  ON  ON  - Color 3 Red Gain
ON  OFF ON  OFF ON  - Rotation (rotates image counterclockwise (-) or
						 clockwise (+))
ON  ON  OFF OFF OFF - PCC-Amp-Fine (narrows or widens the center of the image)
ON  ON  ON  OFF OFF - PCC-Amp (corrects bowed image by narrowing or widening
					the left and right edges).
ON  ON  ON  ON  OFF - PCC-Phase (corrects trapazoid image by narrowing top or
						bottom of image)
ON  ON  ON  ON  ON  - Key-Balance (Corrects a slanted image by moving center
					right or left)
OFF OFF OFF OFF OFF - Pin-Balance (Corrects a distorted image by moving center
					right or left)




