The tool, FreePort Express, is not yet available. Last I looked, it was
scheduled August release. (It was scheduled for July, but seems to have
slipped a bit.)

It is not a compiler, but a binary translator that takes a SunOs 4.1.x
executable and libraries and translates them into Alpha binaries. It is similar
to the DECmigrate software for converting Ultrix and VAX/VMS executables to run
on the Alpha platform.

For information on FreePort Express, see
http://www.novalink.com/freeport-express

Note that the first page says availability will be June 30, 1995, but when you
select that link you get a page that says August.

