In article <3t96ik$mir@no-names.nerdc.ufl.edu>, Christos Siopis <siopis> writes:

>Recently there was a thread on a bug of OSF's cc compiler, regarding the
>-O3 optimization option. I have a problem with the *Fortran* compiler that
>I suspect can be traced back to cc's bug. Here is my problem:
>Assertion failed: 0, file ../../../../../../src/usr/ccs/lib/libmld/
>cmrlc_produce.c, line 864
>0.2u 0.0s 0:00 30% 0+7k 18+8io 1pf+0w
>Fatal error in: /usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/ld IOT/Abort trap 
>fort: Severe: Failed while trying to link.


This is caused by a bug in ld, not cc or f77, relating to "compact relocation 
records". A fix for this is available from Digital, the ID number is OSF320-094.
You can also work around this by using -O1 or the undocumented switch -ncr which
tells ld not to emit compact relocation records.  The disadvantage of -ncr is
that it also prevents you from using pixie or atom to do performance analysis.

