Is it possible you were at a pre-V5 release of VMS the last time the
combination worked?  I've never used the TC03, but I did have a TC02
at the time we ugraded from 4.7 to 5.0, and the "upgrade" caused exactly
the same symptom that you are reporting - the tape drive was
always offline and unmountable.

Emulex released a custom MS: driver so that we could continue using
the TC02 in a Microvax, but I doubt that we have it anymore.  (I now
only use the TC02's in PDP-11's, and I use QT13's/14's in Microvaxen.)
It's possible that you had the Emulex MS: driver for 5.0, but that
it got written over by a later upgrade of VMS.  Of course, you can
always call Emulex (now part of GD California) and see if they still
support the TC series of controllers.  (I know for a fact that they
still support QT's and QD's.)  Their number is (510)417-7000, and the
person I've spoken with regarding QT's and QD's is Eric, x234.  Emulex
also has a BBS (I've only successfully connected to it by forcing my
modem to connect at 2400 baud) at (714)838-5254 which has the latest
revisions of all the manuals.  (If you're at anything but the latest
firmware revision, these manuals may not do you much good.) 

Tim. (shoppa@altair.krl.caltech.edu)



