I'm not sure it is fair to say Noname is the basis of the Linux port
(Linus has an EISA based machine, right now).  However, Noname
currently provides the most cost-effective way to get to an Alpha
running Linux.  As such, most people running Linux/Alpha currently do
so using a Noname board.

Notice that the group in Digital working on Linux/Alpha has switched
to the regular Linux kernel source tree a couple of weeks ago.
Currently, their work is based on 1.2.8 and very soon it should move
up to the latest kernel version (1.3.6 or whatever is current by
then).  Progress is being made fast, so you may wanna check the FAQ at
ftp://cage.cs.arizona.edu/pub/linux/FAQ occasionally to get the latest
status.

