Mike Unverferth (mju@tnt) wrote:
: I have some data files containing values in VAX double-precision.
: I need to convert these values to Intel (IEEE) floating-point.
: Can someone provide the format and/or C code to do the conversion?

The format (D_floating"), is on page 35 of the VAX Architecture Handbook,
and also available in other publications that describe the VAX instruction
set, possibly even in on-line HELP MACRO. The 64-bit data is stored in 4
16-bit words as

sign | 8-bit excess-128 2's exponent | 7-bit ms fraction with 'hidden' bit
16-bit ms-1 fraction
16-bit ms-2 fraction
16-bit ls fraction

