newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.os.vms

I think I missed the early articles in this thread. So I don't know what
was the problem mentioned with the power supply of Alpha AXP
2100's. But as we I had faced some problem with our 2100 m/cs I posting
this article.

We have two 2100 4/200 rackmount models. Within two weeks of delivery,
both their power supplies died. Their was problem in the AC input
section as the fans in the power supply were also not working. Ofcourse
as the m/cs were in warranty, local DEC people arranged quick
replacement (which in India means 6-8 weeks !!). We tried to find out
from DEC what was the cause, but haven't got an answer about that yet.

My analysis was that the max AC input that the power supplies were rated
for was 240V. In India the normal voltage is 230V, which makes the margin
very small. We have UPS system which feeds not only these 2100 m/cs but
a whole lot of other workstations and MPPs and never had any such
problem.

After the incident, we have made separate AC power arrangements for 
the 2100s making sure their input will never exceed 200V. Since then
(Jan 1995) haven't had any trouble.

It was a real surprise that a server class m/c will have such a power
supply failure.

Anyway, we learned our lessons.

